{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted","id":199239,"title":"Othar Tryggvassen, Solar Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-16T14:19:29-07:00","id":199239,"title":"Othar Tryggvassen, Solar Exalted","content":"Let's hypothesize, for a moment, that you're a redeemed Abyssal who's just gone Solar, now freed of the Great Curse and likely one of the most powerful beings in Creation. And with the experiences you've had and your mind clear, you decide that even if the Curse were broken the Celestial Exalted would remain an unacceptable threat to Creation with their existence, that they give too much power to too few people. Solars, Lunars, Sidereals, Infernals, and Abyssals, yourself included, all have to go. Preferably, of course, in a way that allows Creation to survive. We can refer to this hypothetical Solar as Othar.<br /> <br /> Now, the Exaltations themselves, of course, are inassailable. They can be trapped and modified, but not destroyed, and as long as humans exist that meet their qualifications they will continue to latch on to them. Jade Prisons can break, and of course Othar can't trap his own Solar Exaltation in one, which he wants to do. There is, of course, also the matter of the Dragonblooded Exaltations, which while more numerous still give their power to the privileged few. However, they can in theory be the key to defeating the Celestial Exalted once and for all, for no being can have two Exaltations. If every human in the world were a Terrestrial Exalt, the Celestial Exaltations would continue to exist but be stripped of their danger, unable to find a host to possess.<br /> <br /> Othar's task is therefore threefold:<ul><li>Find a method of permanently transforming every human in Creation into a Dragonblooded</li> <li>Ensure the resulting race is up to snuff for dealing with the challenges that will face Creation</li> <li>Eliminate any remaining threats that they will not be able to deal with on their own</li> </ul>Transforming humanity is the one that takes the longest time but can be done in any order, as it requires creating a Dragonblooded line guaranteed to Exalt without being diluted. Possible ways to do this have come up before, such as sponsoring a Dragonblooded to assist them in taking every purchase of Transcendent Gaian Harmony. Once this is done, and a sufficient number of children are seeded, the rest will come naturally without Othar needing to do anything as the Dragonblooded population will slowly increase over millennia until it becomes the norm. In doing so the Immaculate Philosophy will naturally undergo reform, and while there will still be differences in social status based on wealth and political power, the ability of the oppressed to grow more physically and spiritually powerful than their oppressors will ensure that the social order remains mutable. Laden with more conflict than it might be with no Exalted at all, perhaps, but never quashed under one group's heel for long, and this is all that Othar desires.<br /> <br /> Of course, the current Dragonblooded are too weak to deal with many of Creation's needs, such as expanding the borders of Creation to ward off the Wyld, maintaining the Loom of Fate, or performing the highest levels of Sorcery. This requires expanding the Salinan Working to enable all beings regardless of level of Exaltation to be able to access all circles of Sorcery with sufficient training. It also requires creating some equivalent of Wyld-Shaping Technique. In this case the comparative weakness of Terrestrials is a boon, as it can be used to make the resulting Charm not create non-Dragonblooded humans who might accidentally Exalt as a Celestial. Maintaining Fate is a more tricky prospect, as the system requires restructuring to deal with the much higher concentration of Essence-users anyway. Clearly the operating system is in need of an upgrade!<br /> <br /> All this in mind, what else would our gentleman adventurer have to do in order to achieve his mad goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:31:52-07:00","id":199269,"title":"","content":"There's only one real way to ensure that every living person Exalts as a Dragon-Blooded: Kill everyone who isn't. And keep the program up for a few generations to weed out anyone of weak blood.<br /> <br /> Then, develop transcendent charms for Dragon-Blooded. It's a thing that can happen in the rarest of rare cases.<br /> Or, create artifacts that mimic the necessary Charms/Spells, because allowing allowing DBs to transcend allows them to get to the same dangerous power level. <br /> Do not under any circumstances work to allow access to greater Circles of Sorcery, because otherwise one of those damn DBs will break through to Solar Circle somehow, eventually, and then all hell breaks loose again. <br /> Also, to protect creation, use the mass slaughter to run necrotic essence wards through the rim of Creation. That's pretty alien to the Wyld, and should hold it off. <br /> <br /> Of course, Othar is a psychopath who will slaughter just about the entirety of Creation. Meaning there is a simpler solution.<br /> <br /> Destroy Creation, make a new, better one in his own image. Fixing all of those flaws. Maybe even save a few, worthy Dragon-Blooded. Probably a few hundred, tops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:35:36-07:00","id":199286,"title":"","content":"He'd also need to get rid of Lytek because he's gonna be <i>piiiiised.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:53:55-07:00","id":199300,"title":"","content":"I don't think you could get DBs to use SCS in any way. The Salinian Working doesn't let anyone break their natural cap on Sorcery level accessible. It just puts the knowledge into the world itself, rather than in books and treatises, letting people initiate without actually studying. I'd argue an even greater working still wouldn't let DBs use SCS. Their Exaltations simply can't &quot;run the program,&quot; as it were. Well, without being akumatized, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bI also don't think SCS (by itself) is needed to keep the borders and working of Creation running smoothly. Sure SCS helps. But I think that power is more fundamental founded within the Solar Charmset as a whole than to SCS in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:41:05-07:00","id":199358,"title":"","content":"They need to be akumatized <i>and</i> have access to a unique N/A artifact. <br /> <br /> I mean theoretically you could try to rig something up to let them do it, maybe as a large group or something. Get one of each aspect and plug them into some sort of Gaian Resonance Conduit or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:30:50-07:00","id":199394,"title":"","content":"depends on how you want to do it for your game, after learning all the known gaian harmony charms does a 6th purchase turn them into something akin to a devil tiger, is there a better story for something like that than just a charm purchase. what about alchemicals, are they part of your creation and would the othar want them gone as well? a moving ring of alchemical cities on the borders of creation using the protocols that expand creation might be a very good idea and the alchemicals being champions of whatever people they belong seems to go well with the othar's ideas of how the exalted should act","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:33:53-07:00","id":199395,"title":"","content":"Ejtava's solution, scaled back, seems like a reasonable accelerant: kill a bunch of mortals so Othat has less chaff to deal with, in strategic places to create shadowlands that ward off the Wyld. Let's not, however, forget about our Vaderian friends the Deathlords.<br /> At some point, he'll have to go on a rampage through the Underworld smashing up all those Monstrances, lest someone die before they go full Dragon-Blooded and get an offer they can't refuse from the Neverborn. He'll also have to seal off any shadowlands he can, to keep the Deathlords from sending through ghosts to have ghost-blooded children; I believe those children could not themselves exalt, but they might eventually breed out the ghostly blood and have Exaltable mortals once again.<br /> Then, of course, Othar will have to seal off Yu-Shan, after enacting a pogrom to make sure no humans get left behind (IIRC kids destined to exalt as Sidereals get taken up to Heaven for training). As long as we're on the subject of Sidereals, though, isn't there a Resplendent Destiny that gets a dead soul consideration to become a Terrestrial in their next life? That suggests that someone has say in the matter, so all Othar has to do is break into that god's office and take over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:34:09-07:00","id":199396,"title":"","content":"If you manage to set all this up just in time for the Seal to get broken It'll be a fun couple of weeks in Autochtonia, lets say that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:43:42-07:00","id":199401,"title":"","content":"Technically, there is a way to permanently destroy an Exaltation. If he was trying to purge all of creation, heaven, and hell of Celestial Exaltations he'd have to trap them, or possibly their current host, and chuck them into the Abyss. But that would require him leaving one of the biggest threats to Creation unattended, or potentially destroying all the others, tossing the Neverborn in the Abyss as well (in theory then wiping out the Underworld in the process) and then he'd be left with only one singular Celestial Shard left, his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:19:14-07:00","id":199454,"title":"","content":"[ QUOTE=SamuraiMujuru;n199401]Technically, there is a way to permanently destroy an Exaltation. If he was trying to purge all of creation, heaven, and hell of Celestial Exaltations he'd have to trap them, or possibly their current host, and chuck them into the Abyss. But that would require him leaving one of the biggest threats to Creation unattended, or potentially destroying all the others, tossing the Neverborn in the Abyss as well (in theory then wiping out the Underworld in the process) and then he'd be left with only one singular Celestial Shard left, his own.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I thought the exalted shards would fly away if the host died","signature":"","edited":{"userid":359,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","user":"Dezeroth","date":". 07-16-2014, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:50:05-07:00","id":199475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199454#post199454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199401#post199401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, there is a way to permanently destroy an Exaltation. If he was trying to purge all of creation, heaven, and hell of Celestial Exaltations he'd have to trap them, or possibly their current host, and chuck them into the Abyss. But that would require him leaving one of the biggest threats to Creation unattended, or potentially destroying all the others, tossing the Neverborn in the Abyss as well (in theory then wiping out the Underworld in the process) and then he'd be left with only one singular Celestial Shard left, his own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the exalted shards would fly away if the host died</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what i also remember from at least one of the books too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T19:49:44-07:00","id":199563,"title":"","content":"Also remember, anyone left over after Othar's culling will be his spunky girl sidekick. Whether they want to be or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T20:11:29-07:00","id":199575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199475#post199475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what i also remember from at least one of the books too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They do fly away if the host dies, but the Void doesn't kill, it consumes. I'm trying to track down where it mentions that the Void can actually destroy a Shard. IF I recall it's mentioned along with what happens if a Deathlord chucks a Monstrance into the Void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 07-16-2014, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T21:48:00-07:00","id":199662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199395#post199395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as we're on the subject of Sidereals, though, isn't there a Resplendent Destiny that gets a dead soul consideration to become a Terrestrial in their next life? That suggests that someone has say in the matter, so all Othar has to do is break into that god's office and take over.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a God of Terrestrial Exaltation, or perhaps he's the God of Inherited Magic Power (that includes DB Exaltation). He's been doing pretty well since the Usurpation IIRC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199575#post199575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do fly away if the host dies, but the Void doesn't kill, it consumes. I'm trying to track down where it mentions that the Void can actually destroy a Shard. IF I recall it's mentioned along with what happens if a Deathlord chucks a Monstrance into the Void.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Monstrance thing is confirmed to be Deathlord propaganda with no basis in fact. AKA chucking a Monstrance into Oblivion just destroys the Monstrance and makes the Abyssal Exaltation free to choose its own future hosts, versus the host being selected by the Deathlord.<br /> <br /> There's also an old forum saying about how if Creation, Heaven, Hell, the Underworld etc were all plunged into Oblivion and everything in them killed, there would still be 700 Celestial Exaltations forever orbiting Oblivion, just waiting for a living thing to grab on to...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T23:41:15-07:00","id":199715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199662#post199662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also an old forum saying about how if Creation, Heaven, Hell, the Underworld etc were all plunged into Oblivion and everything in them killed, there would still be 700 Celestial Exaltations forever orbiting Oblivion, just waiting for a living thing to grab on to...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually in one of the books, although I forget which one. Celestial Exaltations are pretty much imperishable by any means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T00:23:13-07:00","id":199735,"title":"","content":"Indeed. If the Void is a black hole, then Exaltations are Hawking radiation.<br /> <br /> (I think Othar might want to remain an Abyssal for his project, incidentally. Seems like it might take longer than a Solar's allotted 5000 years or so.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T06:33:50-07:00","id":199951,"title":"","content":"Of course, all of the above will change with the EX3. From what we heard so far, there won't be hard limit on number of exaltations, there will be more types of exalts with their own unique creation modes, and of course there will be exigents of varying powers that could continue to be created long after Othar has offed himself. Basically, to stop new exalts with any degree of certainty, he would have to kill every being capable of creating new ones (so, at least all the remaining Primordials, all the Yozis, all the sronger gods, and possibly the Neverborn as well, just in case). He would also need to kill all the potential hosts - meaning, <i>all of the humans</i>.<br /> Yes, it's a perfect plan, what could be wrong with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:24:26-07:00","id":199991,"title":"","content":"'Course, if <i>anyone</i> is capable of figuring out how to permanently destroy an exaltation, it's a solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:30:20-07:00","id":199999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199735#post199735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I think Othar might want to remain an Abyssal for his project, incidentally. Seems like it might take longer than a Solar's allotted 5000 years or so.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Custom lifespan extending Charms ahoy! Though yeah the feel is much more renegade Abyssal - &quot;I have to kill all these parts of Creation to save it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199951#post199951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, all of the above will change with the EX3. From what we heard so far, there won't be hard limit on number of exaltations, there will be more types of exalts with their own unique creation modes, and of course there will be exigents of varying powers that could continue to be created long after Othar has offed himself. Basically, to stop new exalts with any degree of certainty, he would have to kill every being capable of creating new ones (so, at least all the remaining Primordials, all the Yozis, all the sronger gods, and possibly the Neverborn as well, just in case). He would also need to kill all the potential hosts - meaning, <i>all of the humans</i>.<br /> Yes, it's a perfect plan, what could be wrong with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just humans, anything that has a human-like soul. So beastmen, certain other human-like races, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:35:52-07:00","id":200001,"title":"","content":"Maybe all the animals too, because he's heard this probably-bullshit rumour about the lunar shards and you can't be too careful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T08:19:52-07:00","id":200046,"title":"","content":"Rather than just killing all humans seems like it might be easier to use soul gems or something similar and bind them to automatons if there aren't any natural humanoids there's nothing to exalt and you don't have to deal with moral issues of killing that many people. Also people would probably be OK with being budget alchemicals or at more OK with that than being dead and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/659-dominostro","name":"Dominostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar659_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T08:38:31-07:00","id":200056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199999#post199999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just humans, anything that has a human-like soul. So beastmen, certain other human-like races, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastmen <i>are\u200b </i>human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T08:47:46-07:00","id":200060,"title":"","content":"I'd put money on not everyone on Creation knowing that, mind you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T08:50:14-07:00","id":200063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=200056#post200056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beastmen <i>are\u200b </i>human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I forget that the definition of &quot;human&quot; is pretty broad and most differences that we might consider &quot;a whole different species that can interbreed with us&quot; are basically just phenotypical expression in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T08:57:53-07:00","id":200069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199286#post199286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He'd also need to get rid of Lytek because he's gonna be <i>piiiiised.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And most of the other big gods too. They were really pissed about the chaos losing the Solars caused. Losing every Celestial Exalt? Way worse, and this time they are forewarned. Plus, expect the Gold Faction and the Bronze Faction to table all of their differences, rally the forces of heaven, and react. FAST. you know how the head of the Bureau of Seasons love Solars? Sure, he'll be torn, but if he finds out someone is trying to stomp them out, the aerial legion is coming out, and screw the guy who is doing it, even if he is a Solar.<br /> Not that a dedicated Solar can't overcome these things. Just... people who w","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:03:19-07:00","id":200070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199999#post199999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Custom lifespan extending Charms ahoy! Though yeah the feel is much more renegade Abyssal - &quot;I have to kill all these parts of Creation to save it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Not just humans, anything that has a human-like soul. So beastmen, certain other human-like races, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, technically he is a renegade Abyssals. He just got cleaned up a bit, but that history doesn't just go away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:05:02-07:00","id":200071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=200070#post200070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, technically he is a renegade Abyssals. He just got cleaned up a bit, but that history doesn't just go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically. But he's a Solar again. I'm more saying that the Abyssal Charmset would be more efficient at realizing this goal in some ways, though you'd obviously be lacking access to SCS and VCN is not near as good or applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:06:44-07:00","id":200072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=199735#post199735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. If the Void is a black hole, then Exaltations are Hawking radiation.<br /> <br /> (I think Othar might want to remain an Abyssal for his project, incidentally. Seems like it might take longer than a Solar's allotted 5000 years or so.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, modern theory suggests that the event horizon is permeable from both sides due to quantum tunneling and other effects. If its not permeable, then it creates certain paradoxes which would need to be resolved... sorry, my geek-love for physics came out. Carry on. But yeah, if Oblivion is a black hole, stuff comes out all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:12:32-07:00","id":200076,"title":"","content":"Honestly it may be that completely obliterating creation is the one way to destroy the shards, simply because it will take the very concept of &quot;impossible&quot; with it. <br /> <br /> &quot;You can't destroy us! we're indestru...wait what was that that just fell in?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;indestructibility itself&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;shit&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:17:14-07:00","id":200082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/199239-othar-tryggvassen-solar-exalted?p=200076#post200076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it may be that completely obliterating creation is the one way to destroy the shards, simply because it will take the very concept of &quot;impossible&quot; with it.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't destroy us! we're indestru...wait what was that that just fell in?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;indestructibility itself&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;shit&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, yeah. If you made a direct attack on the shinma, couldn't that destroy base concepts like how things are separate from other things, or how things can be a thing and exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}